  },
  "diagnosis": [
    "The original reader completed preparation, current policy projection and comparison before noticing the writer changed its metadata revision.",
    "The first get_many batch holds immutable hits only within that batch. On retry the shared 64 MiB cache had evicted 7741 structures already held by this same request, so they were prepared again.",
    "The writer race prepared 15483 structures instead of the initial 7742 misses and performed two authority projections and comparisons. This is reproducible wasted work; it is not proof of the exact formal-runner slowdown or deadlock."
  ],
  "repair": [
    "Retain only immutable PreparedToolStructure values in the bounded request, keyed by RegistryToolSnapshot (publication revision plus actual frozen identity). Prune to the current candidates on every retry.",
    "Revalidate configuration and selected Registry version vectors immediately after preparation, before policy projection and comparison.",
    "Keep the fresh database authority transaction, group revision validation and final configuration/Registry checks. No principal, review, grant or visibility result is reused.",
    "Preserve the real 5000-instance/50000-tool scale, shared cache bounds, three-attempt limit, configuration writer budgets and reader.result(timeout=20)."
  ],
